WEBVTT

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.190
Yuno! Yuno!

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:18.070
Wake up or you'll be late for school!

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.080
Mom, give me five more min—

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.800
<i>I've been here for over a year and I'm still not used to this.</i>

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.640
<i>I really miss Mom's miso soup.</i>

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:45.560
<i>Now I'm starting to depress myself a bit.</i>

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.190
<i>Back home, I could always hear Mom in the kitchen when I woke up.</i>

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:57.310
<i>Hiro-san must be cooking.</i>

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.330
<i>Did someone just send a fax?</i>

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.950
<i>Sae-san must have spent the whole night working again.</i>

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:10.710
<i>I can even hear Nori-chan and Nazuna-chan watering the tomatoes.</i>

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.100
Yunocchi, are you awake?

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.480
Morning, Miya-chan! I just woke up!

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.220
youki ni kuchibue fuite

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:54.220
Whistling a cheerful tune

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.550
madobe no kotori to sesshon

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:56.550
I join the birds chirping by the window

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.470
suima ga yatte kite

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:59.470
When fatigue strikes

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.100
atama ga danshingu

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.100
My imagination runs wild

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.560
nan demo kan demo waraeru nichijou

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.560
Everything in life makes me smile

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.400
okimari na kishoutenketsu

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.400
Nothing really new takes place

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.030
demo demo tama ni wa piritto supaisu

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:10.030
But sometimes it's exciting to spice things up

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.650
aozora peintingu

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.650
Let's paint it on the blue sky

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.700
doko ikou

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:13.700
Where should we go?

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.280
koko ni iyou

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.280
Let's stay here

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.280
sore wa nani

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.280
What's that?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.870
are yaritai

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.870
I wanna try that!

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.450
ima ni tokubetsu na shirushi

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:20.450
Let's make this moment count

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.830
tokeibari no mawashikata watashi shidai kamo

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:25.830
How fast my clock moves is all up to me

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.500
shiki oriori iro toridori

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.500
With a rich palette of colors from the four seasons

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.960
nonbiri na everyday

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.960
Our laid-back everyday lives can be

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.590
pasuteru bibiddo metoro

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.590
Any blend of pastel, vivid, and metro colors

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.430
jibun dake no karaaringu

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:37.430
Anyone can create their own coloring

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.010
sono tokidoki mune doki doki

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:40.010
So when your heart races in excitement

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.730
hachamecha na taiyou ni oegaki

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.730
Just draw a sun at the top

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:47.860
tobidasu aatishizumu

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:47.860
And let your inner artist take you from there

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.190
gyutto shite ii kana

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.190
Can I hold your hand tight?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.570
suki suki suki wo sukecchi

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.570
I've been sketching everything I love

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.110
nijiiro ni somete iku yo

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.110
And painting them in rainbow colors

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.870
sore ja ittekimasu

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.870
All right, I'm off to have some more fun!

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.950
May 6th - May 15th

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.950
Japan's a small country,
so where are you going
in such a hurry?

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.480
It's so nice out today!

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.470
I hope this doesn't take too long to dry.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:23.550
Yunocchi!

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:26.220
Oh, Miya-chan, what's up?

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.600
Come here for a sec.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.850
What's going on?

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:37.440
Don't you think it sounds pretty lively down in Sae's room?

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.830
You're right.

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:41.760
Sounds like at least four or five people are down there.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.450
I wonder what they're up to.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.480
I can't really make out what they're saying.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.080
Maybe Sae-san is acting out five roles by herself?

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.080
That would be pretty weird.

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:59.630
Yuno-senpai, Miyako-senpai...
What's the matter?

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.910
We're conducting an investigation!

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:02.560
Huh?

00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:05.680
Sae-san seems to have some guests over.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.720
Did she mention anything about that to you?

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:08.640
No.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.980
You can hear them a little from this room, too.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.730
Not again!

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:22.990
N-Nori-chan probably forgot to save her work and ended up deleting her data.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.450
I'll never get used to her doing that.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.720
I-I see.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.160
I don't think that's related to what we're investigating.

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.400
Yuno-san! Oh, and Miyako-san!

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.710
What's up?

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.470
Nori-chan, did something happen to the data on your computer?

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.800
Oh, you heard me?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:47.970
Sorry for all the noise.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:52.600
We're investigating what's going on in Sae's room.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.000
Sae's room?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.400
It <i>does</i> sound pretty noisy despite how early it is.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.650
Why not just go to Sae's room and see for yourself?

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:03.150
I thought I'd gather some information first.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.910
I can't hear much even though we're right next door.

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.910
Got any high-tech equipment that'll let me hear what's going on next door clearly?

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.790
Did you just ask me for a tapping device?!

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.730
One, two... Five in all, I guess.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.550
Looks like Hiro-san is there, too.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:28.720
Scheduling... a train?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.060
Cold... hotel?

00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:35.060
Um, I probably should've said this earlier, but I don't think we should be doing this.

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:35.560
Well...

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.700
We'll just apologize if they find out.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:41.440
Yeah.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.410
Hey! What are you two snooping around for?!

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.070
Sae-san!

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.670
U-Um, we heard a bunch of voices, so we got a little curious.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:52.580
I'm sorry.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.180
Oh, sorry. Were we being loud?

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:56.250
We'll be done soon.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.080
We don't mind.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.620
Oh, are these two Yuno-chan and Miya-chan?

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:02.740
Y-Yes.

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:03.920
I knew it!

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:05.840
How could you tell?

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.840
Well, Sae and Hiro talk about you guys all the time.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.850
Like how you're so cute and—

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.180
Ah

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.130
See you later.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.170
Take care!

00:06:18.170 --> 00:06:19.690
Bye-bye!

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.940
A school trip?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:26.170
Yeah, it's in ten days.

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:29.060
We're trying to decide what our group should do there.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:30.410
Where are you going?

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:32.580
We're spending three days in Hokkaido.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:37.880
Sae wants to visit a lavender farm and a music box shop.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:39.580
Isn't that cute?

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:42.880
H-Hiro, you said you wanted to go there, too!

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.910
A honeymoon?

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:52.130
You two are lucky. I've never been to Hokkaido.

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:55.010
I hear it's huge.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:58.400
Have you ever been there, Yunocchi?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.580
No, I've never been there either.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.220
I'd like to go, though!

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.190
If I go to Hokkaido...

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.690
I can eat the best baked potatoes in the world with butter, right?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:07.820
Yeah!

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.570
You can get the best scallops with butter, too!

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.400
Wow!

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:20.610
So, where did you all go for your school trip back in middle school?

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:22.720
I visited Kyoto and Nara.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.420
I went to Kyoto and Nara in elementary school, then Hiroshima during middle school.

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:30.800
My school went to Destiny Land.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.690
Whoa, Destiny Land! That must've been really nice.

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.560
What can you learn at an amusement park?

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.600
Huh?

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.800
It's got nothing to do with school.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:44.550
Nori-chan must've never gone there.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.180
I bet she wants to.

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:51.030
Hey, do you think we'll get to visit Hokkaido, too?

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.930
Probably not.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.660
It's different every year.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:57.330
I don't remember where they went for the last two years.

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.960
Well...

00:07:58.960 --> 00:08:00.780
Last year was Okinawa,

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.330
and the year before that was Korea, wasn't it?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:04.700
Oh, that's right.

00:08:04.700 --> 00:08:06.960
But how did you know that?

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:08.960
Um...

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:15.230
I noticed a lot of Yamabuki students using the Okinawan dialect to greet each other last year

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:21.990
and <i>"Annyeonghaseyo"</i> was popular the year before, so I just put two and two together.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:24.480
They really left an impression on you, huh?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.730
Nazuna-chan used to live close to the school, after all.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:30.990
I feel like I need to apologize for some reason.

00:08:32.490 --> 00:08:35.780
Good morning, everyone!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.530
As some of you may already know,

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:42.300
the school trip for third-years is right around the corner!

00:08:42.300 --> 00:08:47.740
Since they'll be going to Hokkaido, I
dressed up as Hokkaido's famous sea urchin!

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.050
Oh, but you can't eat what's inside me!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.800
I've prepared a special lesson for today called "The Charms of Hokkaido".

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.560
I think it'll be a very enlightening lesson, so please enjoy it!

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.420
Carved wooden bears are a symbol often associated with Hokkaido.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.240
I thought about dressing up as a bear, but given the season,

00:09:07.240 --> 00:09:09.900
I'd work up a sweat in no time if I wore fur.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.310
However, if someone really wants to see me dress up,

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:16.200
I'll have the costume ready by the next class!

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:17.910
Is anyone interested?

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:22.200
Anyone?

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.460
That silhouette...

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.670
It's the principal!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.290
Yoshinoya-sensei, please teach the
students what they actually need to learn!

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:39.200
I want to go to Hokkaido, too!

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.530
I'll be a responsible chaperone!

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.570
The faculty members assigned to the third-years are enough.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:47.690
And why are you dressed like a chestnut?

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.040
I'm not a <i>chestnut</i>!

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:50.900
I'm a sea urchin!

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:53.190
They're a special commodity in Hokkaido!

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:54.240
Sea urchin...

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.070
Yunocchi, this trip is going to be amazing.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.700
Only the third-years are going, though.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.990
And you're following us out to shop because...?

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:11.170
Four heads are better than two!

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.330
She has a point.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:17.590
We're less likely to forget to buy something this way.

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:18.930
You really think so?

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.180
Hiro-san! Sae-san!

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:23.930
Buy these, too!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:24.980
For catching salmons!

00:10:24.980 --> 00:10:26.080
And harvesting potatoes!

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.520
You two...

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.690
You think we need to get anything in case of cold weather?

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:35.850
Good call. It might still be cold in Hokkaido.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:37.020
<i>Sae!</i>

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:41.030
Which one do you think looks better on me?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:45.040
<i>The checkered one! The checkered one obviously suits you more!</i>

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:47.120
The checkered one suits you more.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.040
<i>All right!</i>

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.940
Oh, Natsume!

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:57.260
What are you doing here?

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:01.760
S-Sae, I can't imagine what twist of
fate caused me to run into you today.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:02.980
Twist of fate?

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.220
Aren't you here to buy stuff for the school trip, too?

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.710
W-Well...

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:12.900
Of course not! I'm already prepared to go.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.250
I can't believe you're really buying stuff right before the trip!

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:19.860
Make sure you get everything you need!

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.660
Can we make a quick stop at the pharmacy after this?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.750
Sure. What do you need to get?

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.280
Some medicine for motion sickness.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:34.620
We'll be on a plane or a bus for quite a while, won't we?

00:11:34.620 --> 00:11:36.150
So just in case...

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.710
You don't need to get any of that stuff.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.470
Huh? Why not?

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.680
We'll always be together,

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:43.470
so we won't get sick.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:49.540
The way you say things like that so easily...

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:51.090
Huh? What?

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:52.560
Nothing.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:58.820
Now that we've bought everything we need, I'm feeling so stoked for the trip!

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.570
Yeah! I'm looking forward to it, too.

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:06.950
This is the first time you two will be gone for
that long. We're gonna be lonely without you.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.950
Oh, that's right.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:15.630
The average age of the Hidamari Apartment residents will be lower for three days.

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:25.390
I've got my underwear, socks, a guidebook...

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:27.760
Oh, yeah. Some toner and milky lotion.

00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.920
Okay, that should be everything.

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:34.150
I should get to bed early so I can wake up on time tomorrow.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.930
Hiro-san! Hiro-san!
Do you have any extra space in your bags?

00:12:38.930 --> 00:12:40.150
Miya-chan?

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.400
Well, I have a little free space. Why?

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.030
Take this with you.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:49.580
The school trip is tomorrow.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.790
I'm getting excited even though I'm not going.

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.290
Gotta wake up early tomorrow.

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.230
Got everything?

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:01.050
Yeah, I'm all set.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.910
Should we say goodbye to everyone?

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:05.020
It's pretty early. Let's not wake them up.

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.050
Right.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.140
Sae-san! Hiro-san!

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.940
See you!

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:23.940
It's as if they're the ones going on a trip.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:26.950
May 6th - 15th

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:26.950
The End

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:26.950
To be continued

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:31.330
They really left, huh?

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.590
At least it's nice out today.

00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:34.700
Yup.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:41.090
<i>With the third-years on the school trip,
Miya-chan and I are actually the upperclassmen.</i>

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:44.300
<i>We need to pull ourselves together and act like the upperclassmen that we are!</i>

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:47.710
It's still only 7:30, isn't it?

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:49.410
I think I'll get a little more sleep.

00:13:49.410 --> 00:13:51.010
What? You're going back to bed?

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:54.930
I'll make it to school if I wake up around 8:15.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:59.060
15? You'll barely make it on time then!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.320
I-I agree with Nori-chan!

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.320
What?

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:07.320
May 16th - May 18th

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:07.320
The Huge Island o' Hokkaido

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:12.820
The school is so quiet with the third-years gone.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:16.580
Well, yeah. A whole third of the student body is gone.

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:17.330
Oh!

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.270
Yunocchi, go to the classroom without me.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:23.000
Is there something you need to do in the third-year classroom?

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.780
Yeah, sure.

00:14:26.150 --> 00:14:28.340
I'll go, then.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:44.960
What did you do?

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:46.110
A dash.

00:14:48.610 --> 00:14:53.900
I tried to negotiate with them, but they kept
saying that they can't take a second-year teacher.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:57.180
They left me behind!

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:58.250
<i>Who wouldn't?</i>

00:14:58.250 --> 00:15:00.040
I'll remember this!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.000
When I go on school trip with you all next year,

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.290
<i>I'll</i> be the one having fun!

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:13.430
<i>Is there anything I can do for Nori-chan
and Nazuna-chan as an upperclassman?</i>

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:15.890
You're someone I know can always count on, Yuno-senpai.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:17.310
I respect you!

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:18.560
Oh, please!

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.230
Yunocchi, you're amazing!

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:21.480
Come on, now.

00:15:21.480 --> 00:15:23.130
You've really grown, Yuno.

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.730
You're really acting like an upperclassman now.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:29.030
<i>That was probably a little off.</i>

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:38.870
The streets look so cute!

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.240
The air is so fresh!

00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:43.250
We have free time until 3, right?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:47.160
Yeah, we'll visit Orgel Doh, then go to the Glass Studio.

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:50.880
Let's find somewhere nearby to eat lunch, too.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.510
Hiro, are you cold?

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.260
Not as much as I was expecting to be, but yeah.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.220
Oh, ice cream!

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:00.910
I want some!

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.730
Her appetite won.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:08.270
There's so much glass.

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:09.110
They're all beautiful!

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:12.170
These look so cute!

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:13.740
Gonna buy that, Hiro?

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:16.910
You like it, don't you?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.240
What's there to think about?

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:21.790
I wonder if I should get six of these.

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:22.960
That would be expensive.

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.290
I think one or two should be enough.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.480
Hey, let's have lunch here.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:31.900
I'm starving.

00:16:31.900 --> 00:16:33.310
Here?

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:34.710
Western food?

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:37.010
I can't take another step.

00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:42.000
Their best dish is a fried-rice omelette.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:43.600
That sounds absolutely delicious.

00:16:43.600 --> 00:16:45.140
It does, but...

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:48.430
We came all the way to Hokkaido and that's all we're getting?

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:50.960
We should at least order a sashimi rice bowl or something.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:51.900
Here you go.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.660
So good!

00:17:04.160 --> 00:17:05.910
This place is so huge!

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:07.420
The horses are so cute!

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.840
I want to ride them, but the line's so long.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:14.120
Hey, let's ride this!

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:15.810
It's a horseback simulator!

00:17:15.810 --> 00:17:17.760
Sae, give it a try.

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:19.010
What, me?

00:17:21.820 --> 00:17:23.700
Whoa!

00:17:23.700 --> 00:17:25.570
This is too fast!

00:17:29.190 --> 00:17:30.770
Are you filming me?!

00:17:32.270 --> 00:17:33.690
Hiro, delete it!

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.450
Delete it! Give it here!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:37.700
Hiro!

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:42.410
Hey, Sae, look at that.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.830
Huh? What?

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:47.310
It's an alpaca.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:48.920
Isn't it cute?

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:50.450
Sae?

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:53.210
I'm getting déjà vu.

00:17:53.210 --> 00:17:53.990
Huh?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.440
Hey, want some chocolate?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:07.350
Oh, thanks.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:08.230
Want some, Hiro?

00:18:09.730 --> 00:18:11.980
Oh, she fell asleep.

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:22.870
I guess she won't be needing that medicine.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.230
Something an upperclassman would do...

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:35.420
Yuno-san, do you have a minute?

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:40.050
Nori-chan, Nazuna-chan, what's wrong?

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:44.140
Uh... Nazuna tried making beef and potato stew.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:47.640
How can I improve on this?

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.140
All right!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:51.220
Leave it to me!

00:18:56.980 --> 00:19:01.500
I guess you could... try sifting it and washing it with water?

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.990
There's no helping her, is there?

00:19:07.740 --> 00:19:10.250
Nazuna-chan, I've got this!

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.750
You can count on me!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:19.580
I'm hungry!

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:22.450
Miya-chan, wait just a little longer.

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:24.310
All right, let's get started!

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:26.470
I'll be counting on you!

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:33.400
Okay, I'll be turning this meat and potato stew into curry rice.

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:34.700
I see!

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:36.610
I didn't know you could do that!

00:19:43.360 --> 00:19:44.860
Miya-chan, it's done!

00:19:44.860 --> 00:19:45.740
Yay!

00:19:55.000 --> 00:19:56.780
Let's dig in!

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:58.250
<i>Bon appétit!</i>

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:59.500
Bite!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.270
This is... like...

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.260
It tastes like curry at first,

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:13.560
but then there's this sweet taste of mirin and sugar from the meat and potato stew.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:17.270
I've never seen konjac noodles in curry.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:23.470
It's because the base of my stew was too thick!

00:20:23.470 --> 00:20:25.780
Well, it was more than just thick.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:29.240
<i>I wasn't of any help.</i>

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.000
This is so refreshing.

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:43.240
I wonder what special qualities this water has.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.740
My skin feels all smooth now.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.930
Yeah, I know what you mean.

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:50.940
I wonder how the girls at Hidamari Apartments are doing.

00:20:50.940 --> 00:20:53.280
Hiro, it's only our first day away.

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:56.520
They're probably taking a bath right about now, too.

00:20:56.520 --> 00:20:57.800
<i>S-Sae!</i>

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.890
Hey, Natsume, why don't you go over and say hello?

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:04.320
What? Wh-Why would I?

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.530
Come on. You know you want to.

00:21:06.530 --> 00:21:09.130
What? I don't.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:10.050
I'm...

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:14.790
really glad that I'm in Class B with you girls!

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.450
<i>If only you could be this honest with everyone.</i>

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:18.790
Wh-What?

00:21:21.800 --> 00:21:24.050
Hiro, let's get out before we start feeling dizzy.

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:25.050
Yeah.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:29.080
Hey, we're having a pillow fight after everyone's done bathing!

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:30.100
What?

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:33.430
You in?

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.350
I won't go easy on you.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:43.650
I wonder if the third-years are bathing in hot springs right now.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:48.600
In the end, I couldn't act like a true uperclassman today.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:51.620
I really wanted to impress them.

00:22:02.540 --> 00:22:03.970
I have time to redeem myself.

00:22:03.970 --> 00:22:07.920
All right! I'll try harder tomorrow!

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:14.690
Up north, they have

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:17.110
prawn and scallops...

00:22:17.110 --> 00:22:19.740
Crab, shrimp, salmon...

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:21.030
That's a lot of seafood.

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:21.710
Potatoes...

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:22.290
That sounds so good!

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:23.510
I wish I could be at Hokkaido.

00:22:23.510 --> 00:22:26.860
I bet Sae-san and Hiro-san are enjoying the delicacies of the Earth right now.

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:27.640
Oh yeah!

00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:29.940
Why don't we eat like we're in Hokkaido, too?

00:22:29.940 --> 00:22:31.270
Like we're in Hokkaido?

00:22:31.270 --> 00:22:33.070
Like Sapporo ramen.

00:22:33.070 --> 00:22:37.140
Next time is "May 18th to 19th, Yuno-sama from Above."

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:40.660
We'll be waiting at the Hidamari Apartments, so come see us!
